DATA LICENSING

The MIT license above covers the application code. The bundled datasets are
not all under MIT and carry their own licenses, summarized below. See
/sources (or app/sources/page.tsx) for the live, user-facing version.

  - data/conflicts.json — Editorial summaries draw from English Wikipedia
    article leads (CC BY-SA 4.0) and from secondary sources cited per record.
    Wikipedia attributions are preserved in each conflict's `wikipediaUrl`.
    Casualty figures and "importance" rankings are editorial; treat them
    accordingly.

  - data/empires.json — Polygon geometry is a mix of:
      • aourednik / historical-basemaps (CC BY-SA 4.0)
        https://github.com/aourednik/historical-basemaps
      • Natural Earth 10m cultural vectors (public domain)
      • Hand-constructed polygons drawn from scholarly atlases.

  - data/empire-wikipedia.json — Empire summaries fetched from English
    Wikipedia via the public REST API. Reused under CC BY-SA 4.0 with
    attribution preserved on every entry.

  - data/cities.json — Curated; each entry's date range is editorial.

  - Map basemap — © Mapbox · © OpenStreetMap contributors. Subject to the
    Mapbox terms of service and the OpenStreetMap ODbL.

If you redistribute any of the bundled JSON files, retain the relevant
upstream attribution. Contributions to this repository are accepted under
the MIT license for code and CC BY-SA 4.0 for editorial / textual content.
